<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6b0c13d-ace9-58a0-a5ae-835939f481e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541124 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334928" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"190px\">$2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed2f4962-bfe0-5321-8b55-e0e1d5307252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541149 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541161 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541161 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12e96f84-4ccc-56d9-9840-fa21debf2897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541161 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186308692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541179 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541179 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4e8a613a-20ab-5651-b333-3b8eba88b3c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541179 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541183 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "572e3d09-d0c2-5407-860f-33864b8a2c66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541183 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186308723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541191 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541191 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "738edf14-084a-5ae7-b9a0-e0b01debf2b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541191 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541213 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186541183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541213 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b57b6103-080d-5085-b5f9-fa41b8d0bc4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541213 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186541149 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
